# PR agent-reviews loop (orchestrator + sub-agents)

**Tool:** [agent-reviews](https://github.com/pbakaus/agent-reviews) (`npx agent-reviews`). **CI gate:** `finish-pr-context7` script `scripts/inspect_pr_state.py` (cite skill path; do not paste script bodies).

## Roles

- **Orchestrator (this chat):** Tiny context. Shell checks, state file, spawn **one** `generalPurpose` sub-agent per iteration. **Never** implement fixes or load `--expanded` for all comments.
- **Worker (sub-agent):** One theme only (≤3 related comment IDs or one failing check). Fix, test, commit, push, `reply --resolve`, return JSON.

## DONE (orchestrator stops only when all true)

1. `npx agent-reviews --bots-only --unanswered` — no actionable `CODE` / review threads. **Codacy/Codecov issue-list comments** and **Low/Info Codacy inline threads** are not actionable (resolve with won’t-fix or leave informational; see [Codacy triage](#codacy-triage-non-blocking-lows)).
2. `inspect_pr_state.py` — `failing_checks` empty **or** only non-blocking Codacy noise (pending OK). A red **Codacy** GitHub check alone does **not** block DONE when blocking severities are clear (see Codacy triage).
3. Last worker: `status` `done` or `no_changes` with push if code changed.

**Not done:** one commit, one watch cycle, or “most comments replied.”

## Codacy triage (non-blocking lows)

**PR loop gate:** **Low** and **Info** Codacy findings do **not** block merge readiness. Do not spawn workers or keep the loop open solely to clear them.

| Treat as blocking (fix or escalate) | Treat as non-blocking (no code churn) |
| --- | --- |
| Critical, High, Medium | Low, Info |
| Security / SRM items | Style-only or metric noise (coverage, duplication) |
| Confirmed bugs in touched code | Generic framework analyzer noise covered by `.biome.json` |
| | Generic analyzer noise when [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) / app rules say won’t fix |

**Comments:** Parse severity from the Codacy bot body when present. **Low/Info** → `npx agent-reviews --reply <id> "Won't fix: low Codacy severity; …" --resolve` (cite app rule if applicable). **Medium+** → fix only when valid; same for security.

**Failing Codacy check:** If `inspect_pr_state.py` lists Codacy in `failing_checks`, confirm blocking issues are gone before treating the PR as blocked — e.g. Codacy MCP `codacy_list_pull_request_issues` (`status: new`) or the PR Issues UI. If only Low/Info (or zero new issues) remain, record `codacy_non_blocking: true` in loop state and continue; do **not** treat that check as a work unit.

**Align with:** [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) `Static Analysis` (security and real bugs first; app rules win over generic smells).

## State file (outside repo)

`~/.codex/tmp/finish-pr-context7/<owner>-<repo>-<pr>.json` — or `write_loop_state.py` from finish-pr-context7 skill.

Track: `loop`, `last_commit`, `processed_comment_ids`, `failing_checks`, `codacy_non_blocking`, `status`.

## Orchestrator loop

1. Parallel: `agent-reviews --bots-only --unanswered` + `inspect_pr_state.py --repo "." --pr <N>`.
2. If DONE → stop with summary.
3. Pick **one** work unit (priority): failing CI (skip non-blocking Codacy-only failures) → oldest actionable CODE comment cluster (same file/theme; skip Low/Info Codacy).
4. Increment `loop`; spawn sub-agent with worker prompt (below).
5. Merge worker JSON into state; goto 1. **Do not stop** after one worker unless DONE or `blocked`.

Workers **do not** run `--watch`. Orchestrator may use `--watch --timeout 600` once per session between loops only for required CI/checks or an active CodeRabbit review that is already running. Do not watch for CodeRabbit no-start/skipped/rate-limit/credit/auth/service states; mark CodeRabbit unavailable and rely on local sub-agent review unless actionable CodeRabbit comments already exist.

## Worker prompt (fill placeholders)

```
Worker iteration {LOOP_N}. Repo: {ABS_REPO_PATH}. Branch: {BRANCH}. Last commit: {LAST_COMMIT}.
Theme: {THEME}. Comment IDs: {COMMENT_IDS}. Failing check: {FAILING_CHECK or none}.

Scope only the above. Cite .cursor/rules and AGENTS.md by path. Context7: 3 passes when library/API behavior matters.
Verify each finding; minimal fix. Codacy Low/Info: won't-fix + --resolve, no code change (see pr-agent-reviews-loop Codacy triage). Medium+ / security: fix when valid.
Tests: targeted npm run test, then check:types + lint (+ check:i18n if copy).
Commit + push if changed. Per ID: npx agent-reviews --reply <id> "Fixed in <hash>. …" --resolve OR "Won't fix: …" --resolve.
Use --detail <id> only for assigned IDs. No --watch. No full PR diff.

Return only JSON:
{"status":"done|no_changes|blocked","commit":"<short-hash|null>","fixed_ids":[],"wont_fix_ids":[],"tests_run":[],"blocker":null}
```

## Repo commands (workers)

Only `npm run` scripts from [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md). App rules win over generic bot suggestions — see `pavilion-reservation-pricing.mdc`, `sonarqube-review.mdc`, etc.
